<title>JAPAN: Mitsui Mining to cut zinc price by 5,000.</title>
<headline>Mitsui Mining to cut zinc price by 5,000.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mitsui Mining and Smelting Co said on Tuesday it was cutting its selling price for zinc by 5,000 yen to 190,000 yen per tonne, effective immediately.</p>
<p>A Mitsui Mining official said the cut would make the average zinc price for this month to 191,400 yen.</p>
<p>Major Japanese smelters periodically review their selling prices, changing them in line with market prices and currency rates.</p>
</text>
